index 8db7180..5e80048 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -72,6 +72,49 @@ allowing distros to provide a sane default but also users to change that default
 
 - **storage\_path** (String): path to the image to serve, for example: `/data/myimage.iso`
 
+### Section gadget
+
+Board vendors can override USB device and configuration descriptors without
+changing usb-signaller. Put these settings in a `*.toml` drop-in below
+`/etc/usb-signaller.d/` so distro defaults remain intact.
+
+- **manufacturer** (String): manufacturer string shared by all USB modes.
+- **serialnumber** (String): serial number string shared by all USB modes. If
+  omitted, usb-signaller uses the first device-tree compatible string.
+
+The following optional keys are available in each mode table:
+`[gadget.developer]`, `[gadget.tethering]`, `[gadget.mtp]`,
+`[gadget.accessory]` and `[gadget.mass_storage]`.
+
+- **id\_vendor** / **id\_product** (Integer): USB vendor and product IDs.
+- **product** (String): USB product string.
+- **configuration** (String): configuration description.
+- **device\_class** / **device\_subclass** / **device\_protocol** (Integer):
+  device descriptor class triple. Composite network functions commonly use
+  `0xef`, `0x02`, `0x01`.
+- **max\_power** (Integer): configuration `MaxPower` in milliamperes.
+- **ncm\_qmult** (Integer): NCM function `qmult` for NCM developer and
+  tethering gadgets.
+
+Example board override:
+
+```toml
+[gadget]
+manufacturer = "Example"
+serialnumber = "example-device"
+
+[gadget.developer]
+id_vendor = 0x0525
+id_product = 0xa4a1
+product = "Example NCM"
+configuration = "Example NCM"
+device_class = 0xef
+device_subclass = 0x02
+device_protocol = 0x01
+max_power = 500
+ncm_qmult = 20
+```
+
 ## USB modes
 
 The following USB modes are available:
